## 6. Technology check (MUST)

From requirements + README + `package.json`, list every technology (React, Next.js, Knex, MySQL, Formik, Shopify, etc.).

| Step | Action |
|------|--------|
| Map | Each tech → `.cursor/rules/*-stack.mdc` + `.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md` |
| Conflict | If requirements say Next.js but rules say webpack-only → note in plan; follow **user/requirements** unless rules are stricter for this repo template |
| Missing skill | Load matching skill before implementation |

**MUST** implement according to **technologies named in requirements**, not a default stack from examples.

---

## 7. Research + marketplace tools (before plan / subagents execute)

For each requirement point that is **unclear**, **mandatory but unfamiliar**, or **version-sensitive**:

| Order | Source | When |
|-------|--------|------|
| 1 | **context7 MCP** | Official docs for libraries/APIs in requirements |
| 2 | **Web search** | No context7 hit, integration quirks, errors, third-party setup |
| 3 | **Marketplace & tooling** | See § 7a — **MUST** check before custom-building |
| 4 | **Codebase** | Existing patterns, `.cursor/skills/`, enabled MCP in `{monorepo}` |

- **MUST** research **before** writing implementation steps when the requirement needs external knowledge.
- **MUST** record findings in plan § Research notes **and** § Tools & marketplace (master or feature chunk).

### 7a. Marketplace & available tools (MUST during research)

Before inventing a custom solution, **check what already exists**:

| Check | Where | Look for |
|-------|-------|----------|
| Cursor **skills** | `.cursor/skills/`, `app/backend/src/assets/cursor/skills/` (template) | Matching workflow (Figma, MySQL, planning, etc.) |
| Cursor **rules** | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Stack standards already copied to project |
| Cursor **agents** | `.cursor/agents/*.md` | `plan-execute`, specialists |
| **MCP servers** | Cursor MCP marketplace, project MCP config (`.cursor/mcp.json`) | Figma, context7, Playwright, GitHub, etc. |
| **Plugins / extensions** | Cursor marketplace, README “tools” section | Lint, review, design plugins |
| **npm / package registry** | `package.json`, web search | Libraries (Formik, Yup, Knex, etc.) |
| **Monorepo packages** | `packages/*`, existing `{frontend_app}` / `{backend_app}` deps | Reuse before new install |

**Decision rule:**

| Found suitable tool | Not found |
|---------------------|-----------|
| **MUST** add to plan § Tools & marketplace with name, purpose, install/enable step | Document “build custom” + why no marketplace fit |
| Prefer **existing MCP/skill/plugin** over one-off scripts | Web search included “{task} cursor mcp”, “{task} npm library” |

**MUST NOT** skip marketplace check when research runs — even if context7 answered the API question.

Example plan rows:

```markdown
## Tools & marketplace
| Need | Tool | Source | Action |
|------|------|--------|--------|
| Figma → code | Figma MCP + figma-tree-todo skill | Cursor MCP / `.cursor/skills/` | Use existing — load skill before MCP |
| Form validation | formik + yup | npm | Add to `{frontend_app}` if not in package.json |
| DB migrations | Knex (already in `{backend_app}`) | codebase | Reuse — no new tool |
| OAuth | (none in MCP) | web search | Custom impl per docs; note gap |
```

- If a marketplace tool **should** be added to the project (MCP entry, npm dep, skill copy), put it in the **first milestone** of the relevant feature chunk.
- **MUST** ask user before adding paid or broad-permission marketplace plugins unless README/docs already allow.

